2. Multiple Inheritance

Definition

    Multiple inheritance means, One child class inherits from more than one parent class.

        Teacher      Employee
              \      /
               \    /
               CollegeStaff

Does Java Support It?
    No.

    Java does NOT support Multiple Inheritance using classes.

    Java supports it only through Interfaces.

Why?

    Because of the Diamond Problem.

Suppose

            Person
           /      \
     Teacher      Employee
           \      /
          CollegeStaff

    Both Teacher and Employee have

    display();

    Now,

    CollegeStaff.display();

    Which display() should execute?

    Teacher's?

    or

    Employee's?

    Java cannot decide.

    This creates ambiguity.

    Hence Java avoids it.

    Diamond Problem
                 Person
                display()

                /      \
               /        \

     Teacher             Employee
     display()           display()

               \        /

                \      /

             CollegeStaff

    Ambiguous call

    staff.display();

    Which method?

        Teacher?

        Employee?